  "slug": "decoding-pathology-17b5",
  "summary": "Loki2, GenVinci and sc-HistoMorphomics treat routine H&E as a molecular readout, as Bloom, MCT and scUNVEIL scale cell representation learning.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational recovery of molecular state from tissue and cell data. Three preprints use H&E as a molecular readout. Loki2, trained on 15 million cells, tests how much molecular and cellular state histology encodes. GenVinci reconstructs 3D molecular tissue scenes and maps senescence across aging mouse organs and human skin. sc-HistoMorphomics links 194 nuclear morphometric features to spatial transcriptomics. In parallel, foundation models expand cell representation learning. Bloom unifies expression and chromatin accessibility across 300,000 mouse brain cells. MCT models cell sets to learn context-aware gene co-regulation. scUNVEIL pretrains on about 92 million human cells via next-UMI prediction. Spatial analysis tools include CIRCA, which uses causal representation learning to recover identifiable cell and niche programs, and spicyR v2, a permutation-free co-localisation test with sample-size estimation. Other work addresses dynamics and reliability: GFM for unseen perturbation responses, DRAFT for dynamic GRNs, GatorAnchor for neighborhood uncertainty, and SigMatch on tissue bias in disease-relationship predictions.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
